# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads to Cloud Build.
#
# This is a SEPARATE mechanism from .dockerignore. .dockerignore trims what the
# docker daemon sees as build context; .gcloudignore trims what gcloud uploads in
# the first place. Without this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore, which meant
# the whole test suite, its fixtures and every doc were being shipped to the build.
#
# Keep in step with .dockerignore. Anything the image needs at build time must NOT
# be listed here — in particular backend/, frontend/ and backend/data/collections.json.

.git
.gitignore
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
static

# Tests, fixtures and dev tooling — the image does not run them.
backend/tests
backend/scripts/bench_elevation.py
pytest.ini
.claude

# Local artifacts and scratch output.
backend/_cache_twins.pkl
routes.geojson
**/.cache
.DS_Store

# Docs and planning notes.
docs
*.md
Sick Slopes.zip
_unzipped
cpp

# Local road-network snapshots (data/). The `all`-tier GOL built for local dev is
# ~820 MB and must never reach the build: it would be uploaded to Cloud Build on
# every deploy and, if it landed in the image, would ship 34 regions' worth of
# cold-start pull time. Only the deploy-tier file is allowed through.
#
# Note the ordering: exclude everything in data/, then re-admit the deploy GOL,
# its manifest, and the .keep sentinel the Dockerfile's COPY needs.
data/*
!data/.keep
!data/hillbomb-deploy.gol
!data/hillbomb-deploy.gol.regions.json
